<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/specifications/level4-ecdf-lesson> {
  ex:l4-ecdf-small-chart cd:interactiveObservations false .
  ex:l4-ecdf-river-chart cd:interactiveObservations false .
  ex:l4-ecdf-shapes-chart cd:interactiveObservations false .
  ex:l4-ecdf-question a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "A bin-free view of the frequency distribution?"@en ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Same data, different histograms**\n\nBin width and origin change the picture, not the data. We want an empirical distribution view **without those choices**.\n\n- **Parameter-free counting:** no bins, bandwidth or assumed distribution family.\n- **Cumulative:** at each value, report the fraction **at or below it**.\n- **Objective for the same data:** no subjective bin selection; sampling bias and measurement limits remain.\n\n==The ECDF accumulates frequencies. It is not a density curve.=="@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-ecdf-concept a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "ECDF: one cumulative count for every threshold"@en ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Empirical cumulative distribution function**\n\nFor each x, count every observation with xᵢ ≤ x and divide by n. The indicator in the formula is **1 when the condition holds, otherwise 0**.\n\n- Sort the data, retaining identities and ties.\n- At each observed value, add its multiplicity/n.\n- Hold the fraction constant until the next value.\n\n==No bins, no fitted population model.== Below the minimum the ECDF is 0; at and above the maximum it is 1. It includes the jump at x: **right-continuity**."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-ecdf-worked a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Calculate an ECDF: include every tie"@en ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Seven-value hand calculation**\n\nSorted synthetic concentrations: **2, 4, 4, 5, 5, 6, 7 mg/L**.\n\n- At x = 3.9: 1 value included → **1/7**.\n- At x = 4: both tied 4s enter → **3/7**.\n- At x = 4.1: no new value → still **3/7**.\n\nThe jump at 4 is **2/7**, not 1/7. Filled endpoints are included; open endpoints are left limits. The vertical connector is not a set of intermediate function values."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-ecdf-small-chart a cd:ChartDefinition ; cd:chartType cd:ObservationExplorer ; cd:observationView "ecdf" ; cd:compactObservations true ; skos:prefLabel "Two tied values enter at x = 4"@en ; cd:body "At x = 4 mg/L, the two tied values enter together: Fₙ(4) = 3/7."@en ; cd:xAxisLabel "Threshold x"@en ; cd:xAxisUnit "mg/L" ; cd:yAxisLabel "Fₙ(x)"@en ; cd:thresholdMinimum 0.0 ; cd:thresholdMaximum 8.0 ; cd:thresholdInitial 4.0 ; cd:thresholdStep 0.1 ; cd:hasObservationSeries ex:l4-observation-reference ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l4-ecdf-river a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Answer the river question exactly"@en ; cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ; cd:body "**Scenario**\n\n50 constructed river concentrations: 0.5, 1.0, …, 25.0 mg/L. Not environmental evidence.\n\n**Interpretation**\n\nAt **12.3 mg/L**, 24 observations are included: **24/50 = 48%**. There are no observations between 12 and 12.5, so this segment is flat.\n\nAt 12.5: **25/50 = 50%**. For an interval (a,b], subtract Fₙ(a) from Fₙ(b). This is an observed sample fraction, not an estimate with guaranteed precision or a regulatory conclusion."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
